# Design: the word lens, the first lens written in form. The page spec/lens.md is the authority; these nodes say what it chose and why.

n: 5.15
name: word-lens
kind: hub
is: The first lens: words beside the catalogue's numbers and the common leaves written as people write them, read forwards into nodes and shown backwards as text by one module written in form. The canonical print stays what is stored. It is the first step of the home lens of 5.3.5 and not that lens: it has rows of words only.
at: 2026-11-25

n: 5.15.1
name: words-are-rows-beside-the-nodes
kind: decision
is: An entry's word is a row, a word and the entry it names, in a list a bound entry answers (lens/words.ck). No node holds its own word, so renaming changes no id and a second lexicon can name the same entries otherwise. Entries below 128 are named by the bootstrap's pages; from 128 up by modules written in form, and 129 to 161 are the lens's own.
status: inferred
from: 5.3.2 5.13.3 5.1.5
src: 2.30.14 2.30.15
conf: mid
limit: No row yet says which numbers a module may take; the lens's range is a convention of its page.
at: 2026-11-25

n: 5.15.2
name: showing-is-total-and-reading-inverts-it
kind: decision
is: The lens shows every node: a word or #N for an entry, a number for a short int or nat, quotes for a plain text, brackets with hex for every other leaf, and brackets around a blueprint and its children for a composite. Reading takes all of these and gives back the node that was shown. A node written twice is one node, so sharing needs no mark. Text it cannot read is a fault whose reason is a word and the place.
status: inferred
from: 5.3.3 5.3.8 5.3.4 5.14.31
src: 2.30.14 2.30.15
conf: mid
why: The notation is the one the observer already prints, so what is watched and what is written look the same.
flip: A node with much sharing shows long; naming a part and using it twice needs a row the lens does not have.
at: 2026-11-25

n: 5.15.3
name: the-lens-reads-its-own-definition
kind: observation
is: Observed on 2026-11-25. The lens was brought into being once, by substituting numbers for words in its source. It then showed its own stored node as 8,197 bytes of text and read that text back to the same canonical print, byte for byte. ground/lens-round-trip.ck, the first program written in words, shows and reads back each of the 50 files of nodes in the repository and names none that differs, in 0.08 s and 14 million walker steps. Six malformed texts each faulted with a word and a place.
status: observed
src: 2.30.14 2.30.15 2.30.7
limit: The list of files is written into the program, so a new file is not covered until it is added. One machine.
at: 2026-11-25
